> can anyone give me some general tips on playing a tourist? I just started
> one and seem to have had abit of luck: GDSM, boots of speed, cloak of
> invisibility, magic bane, vorpal blade (I'm only on Dlvl5).  The only
> problem is this character doesn't seem to be able to destroy everything he
> comes across like barbarians can. Anyway how do I keep this character from
> dying? (aside from not doing stupid things with cockatrices)

Quiver your darts and lob them at tough monsters to soften them up.  
Run away a lot.  With speed boots and invisibility, this shouldn't be
too tough.
Use your camera to blind monsters.  
Keep your pet (you do still have a pet, right?) near you, let it/them
take out the weaker monsters to build up levels.
Don't "save items for later".  Dead characters read no scrolls, quaff
no potions, zap no wands, etc.

Right now, you should have an AC no worse than 1 (+0 GDSM,
burnt/rusted +0 speed boots, burnt cloak of invisibility), and
probably a bit better...  One option is to get to minetown as quickly
as possible (and as low level) to buy cheap protection.

